From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Brue <ryanbrue.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 21:59:42 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 36/58] PROTOTYPE pco: keep the helper test for multisampled
 and A2C shaders

Local experiment for the shared amazon-suez/amazon-sheldonp stack, never to
be sent (Imagination declines LLM-generated code in src/imagination).

The no-ISP-feedback change dropped the helper-invocation test whenever a
fragment shader could not demote or terminate. A multisampled pipeline
whose API sample mask leaves out samples, or alpha to coverage, can still
need it. Keep it in those cases, as amazon-sheldonp's version of the
change (its local patch 0029) did, and pass the static sample count to the
compiler (fs.rasterization_samples was never set; from its local patch
0028), 0 when unknown or dynamic.

0029 also kept it for per-sample shaders. That is not taken: with one
sample, per-sample execution is per-pixel, and nir_lower_blend sets
uses_sample_shading on every shader that reads the destination, so every
blended layer kept the test and ran punch-through (GX6250, gles-layers,
interleaved: textured layer 4.22 -> 5.70 ms, colour quad 3.39 -> 4.98 ms
with that guard).

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 src/imagination/pco/pco_nir_pvfio.c        | 16 ++++++++++++----
 src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_arch_pipeline.c |  9 +++++++++
 2 files changed, 21 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/imagination/pco/pco_nir_pvfio.c b/src/imagination/pco/pco_nir_pvfio.c
index f164b89e367..03ea2ebb1e4 100644
--- a/src/imagination/pco/pco_nir_pvfio.c
+++ b/src/imagination/pco/pco_nir_pvfio.c
@@ -585,10 +585,18 @@ static bool lower_isp_fb(nir_builder *b, struct pfo_state *state)
     * (a sample-mask/sample-id sequence) and an ISP feedback, and ran as a
     * punch-through pass. SUEZ_PCO_ALWAYS_ISP_FB=1 restores that.
     */
-   nir_def *discard_cond = (shader_can_discard(shader) ||
-                            getenv("SUEZ_PCO_ALWAYS_ISP_FB"))
-                              ? nir_is_helper_invocation(b, 1)
-                              : NULL;
+   /* Only drop it where no sample can be killed for the shader either:
+    * single-sampled (known statically) and no alpha to coverage (from
+    * amazon-sheldonp's version of this change). Per-sample execution is no
+    * reason on its own: with one sample it is per-pixel, and nir_lower_blend
+    * marks every shader that reads the destination as per-sample.
+    */
+   const bool keep_helper_test = shader_can_discard(shader) ||
+                                 state->fs->rasterization_samples != 1 ||
+                                 state->fs->uses.alpha_to_coverage ||
+                                 getenv("SUEZ_PCO_ALWAYS_ISP_FB");
+   nir_def *discard_cond =
+      keep_helper_test ? nir_is_helper_invocation(b, 1) : NULL;
 
    /* Drop depth writes and discard cond if early fragment tests. */
    if (shader->info.fs.early_fragment_tests) {
diff --git a/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_arch_pipeline.c b/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_arch_pipeline.c
index 1775f22f248..110ca2ae372 100644
--- a/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_arch_pipeline.c
+++ b/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_arch_pipeline.c
@@ -2530,6 +2530,15 @@ pvr_preprocess_shader_data(pco_data *data,
          (~state->ms->sample_mask &
           BITFIELD_MASK(state->ms->rasterization_samples));
 
+      /* The static sample count, so the compiler can tell a single-sampled
+       * pipeline (0 = unknown or dynamic: assume multisampled).
+       */
+      data->fs.rasterization_samples = 0;
+      if (state->ms &&
+          !BITSET_TEST(state->dynamic,
+                       MESA_VK_DYNAMIC_MS_RASTERIZATION_SAMPLES))
+         data->fs.rasterization_samples = state->ms->rasterization_samples;
+
       if (BITSET_TEST(state->dynamic, MESA_VK_DYNAMIC_CB_COLOR_WRITE_ENABLES) ||
           (state->cb && state->cb->color_write_enables !=
                            BITFIELD_MASK(MESA_VK_MAX_COLOR_ATTACHMENTS))) {
